(a) Final plat format. The final plat shall be clearly and legibly drawn in permanent ink on high-quality reproducible material. Sheet sizes shall be 17 inches by 22 inches. Where more than one sheet is required, all sheets shall be numbered consecutively and shall include a notation of the total number of sheets (i.e., sheet 12 of 13 and the like). The final plat shall be drawn at a scale not smaller than one inch equals 100 feet unless approved otherwise by the Director.
(b) Final plat contents. The final plat shall include the contents of and conform to the general concept of the preliminary plat, with the following additions:
(1) An index map if more than one sheet is required to depict the plat;
(2) The name, address and phone number of all owners of the property to be subdivided;
(3) Identification of the district, land lot and acreage of the property to be subdivided;
(4) A north arrow;
(5) Building setback lines;
(6) A list of all lots and the square footage or each;
(7) A notation of the panel number from floodplain maps;
(8) The name, address and phone number, registration number and seal of the engineer or surveyor who prepared the plat. Additionally, the engineer or surveyor's stamp and original signature must be on each sheet;
(9) Notation that the property being subdivided is located in the City;
(10) Direction and distance from a point on the boundary of the subdivision (subdivision monument) to at least one specific point of reference (City monument). All final plats shall depict the exact boundary lines of the tract by bearings and distances. Such depiction shall include the individual identification indicator, elevation and Georgia State Plane (West) coordinates of each such City monument identified. The location of all such City monuments shall be supplied to any interested party by the Department upon request. These requirements shall specifically apply to all acquisitions of land by the City, except those solely for the purpose of acquiring rights-of-way or for acquiring easements (permanent or temporary). All plats or surveys contracted by or paid for by the City must include the appropriate monument data as required by this chapter;
(11) Municipal, County and land lot lines accurately tied to the lines of the subdivision by distance and bearings where these lines traverse or are reasonably close to the subdivision;
(12) Exact boundary lines of the tract, determined by a field survey, giving distances to the nearest 100th foot and bearing to the nearest second, which shall be balanced and closed with an error of closure not less than 1:10,000;
(13) Name of subdivision, exact locations, right-of-way widths, pavement widths, and names of all streets and alleys within and immediately adjoining plat;
(14) Street centerlines;
(15) Lot lines, with dimensions to the nearest 100th foot, and bearings;
(16) Lots numbered in numerical order;
